<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<root>
  <!--
    Homespool's shared strings, in the neutral language (English).

    Naming: Area_Thing. A key is never the English text itself - an English-keyed resource means
    changing the wording changes the key, which silently orphans every translation of it.

    Plural keys come in pairs, Thing_One and Thing_Other, and are read through Plural.Format rather
    than by looking one up directly. See Plural.cs for why the pair is the minimum and why more
    forms are a per-language matter.

    Nothing machine-facing belongs here: CSS class names, protocol values, gcode, filenames and
    go2rtc source strings are not text a person reads, and localising one produces a value another
    system rejects. See notes/localisation.md.
  -->
